.TH atrun 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
atrun \- run the jobs queued by at
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B atrun
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR at (1)
does not run anything itself: it writes a file into the spool directory
naming the time.
.B atrun
looks through that directory and runs whatever is now due.
.PP
It is meant to be run once a minute from
.BR cron (1),
and is of no use typed by hand except to flush the queue.
.SH NOTES
Since
.B cron
is not started on this machine as shipped, nothing runs
.B atrun
either, and a job queued with
.B at
sits there until something does.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR at (1),
.BR cron (1)
